revision.text:
[[File:Sumiyosihakata01.jpg|thumb|right|Tprii at Sumiyoshi shrine entrance]]
{{nihongo|'''Sumiyoshi-jinja'''|住吉神社||}} is the [[Japan]]ese [[Shinto shrine]] at [[Hakata, Fukuoka|Hakata]] in [[Fukuoka Prefecture]] on the island of [[Kyushu]].<ref name="kotodamayama">Kotodamaya.com, [http://www.kotodamaya.com/sumiyoshi-jinja/ "Sumiyoshi Jinja"]; retrieved 2012-10-28.</ref>
==History== ''Sumiyoshi'' was one of the chief Shinto shrines (''[[ichinomiya]]'') of the old [[Chikuzen Province]]. It serves today as one of the ''ichinomiya'' of [[Fukuoka Prefecture]].<ref>[http://eos.kokugakuin.ac.jp/modules/xwords/images/uploads/EOS070712Ab.pdf "Nationwide List of ''Ichinomiya''," p. 2]; retrieved 2012-10-28.</ref> The enshrined ''[[kami]]'' are: * {{nihongo|Sokotsutsunoo no mikoto|底筒男命||}}<ref name="kotodamayama"/> * {{nihongo|Nakatsutsunoo no mikoto|中筒男命||}}<ref name="kotodamayama"/> * {{nihongo|Uhatsutsunoo no mikoto|表筒男命)||}}<ref name="kotodamayama"/>
==References== {{reflist}}
==Other websites== {{Commons category-inline|Sumiyoshi-jinja (Fukuoka)}}
